Subject: [PATCH 05/10] [3.1.2] [M156] Handle RenderProcessHost destruction in
 ChromePluginServiceFilter

Original change's description:
> Handle RenderProcessHost destruction in ChromePluginServiceFilter
>
> ChromePluginServiceFilter observes RenderProcessHost instances to clear
> authorized plugin state and observations when processes terminate.
> It only implemented RenderProcessHostObserver::RenderProcessExited(), so
> if a renderer process exits before ObserveRenderProcessHost executes on
> the UI thread, RenderProcessExited() gets skipped during subsequent host
> cleanup, which only dispatches RenderProcessHostDestroyed().
>
> Address this gap by overriding RenderProcessHostDestroyed() to ensure
> observations and process details are cleared whenever an observed host
> is deleted.
>
